<?php require_once __DIR__.'/../../includes/functions.php';$slug=basename(__DIR__);$article=null;foreach(article_data() as $a){if($a['slug']===$slug){$article=$a;break;}}if(!$article){http_response_code(404);exit('Not found');}$title=$article['title'].' | Mid City Home Restoration';$description=$article['excerpt'];include __DIR__.'/../../includes/header.php';$recent=array_slice(array_filter(article_data(),fn($x)=>$x['slug']!==$slug),0,5);?><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow"><?=e(date('F j, Y',strtotime($article['date'])))?> · Project Planning</p><h1><?=e($article['title'])?></h1><p class="lead"><?=e($article['excerpt'])?></p></div></section><section class="section white"><div class="wrap content-grid"><article class="rich"><img src="<?=e($article['image'])?>" alt="<?=e($article['title'])?>"><h2>Start with the outcome, not the shopping list</h2><p>A strong renovation plan begins with the problem the property needs to solve. Clarify who will use the space, what is failing now, what must stay, and what “finished” should mean before discussing products.</p><h2>Translate the goal into a written scope</h2><p>The scope should define demolition, protection, preparation, installation, licensed trade work, finish standards, exclusions, and cleanup. Ambiguity at this stage becomes delay or cost later.</p><h2>Lock critical decisions before work starts</h2><p>Materials with long lead times, layout choices, fixtures, and finish details should be approved before demolition whenever possible. This keeps the project sequence predictable and reduces rushed substitutions.</p><h2>Document progress and changes</h2><p>Photos, written approvals, and clear change orders protect both the property owner and contractor. The goal is not more paperwork; it is fewer misunderstandings.</p><h2>Close the project with verification</h2><p>A final walkthrough, punch list, completion record, and warranty information create a clean handoff and confirm the work against the agreed scope.</p><div class="form-card" style="margin-top:45px"><p class="eyebrow">Need a site-specific plan?</p><h2>Book an on-site assessment.</h2><p>We will turn the property need into a clear, written project scope.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Request a Site Visit</a></div></article><aside class="sidebar"><div class="widget"><h3>Recent posts</h3><?php foreach($recent as $r):?><a href="/articles/<?=e($r['slug'])?>/"><?=e($r['title'])?></a><?php endforeach;?></div><div class="widget"><h3>Plan your project</h3><p>Get a detailed assessment and written estimate.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Start Here</a></div></aside></div></section><?php include __DIR__.'/../../includes/footer.php';?>